    "originalTitleEn": "Linh's secret to reaching from domestic Android Engineer to Software Engineer Tik Tok",
    "originalHtmlEn": "<h2>Linh's secret to reaching from domestic Android Engineer to Software Engineer Tik Tok</h2><p>In the context of large technology companies such as TikTok, Google or Amazon becoming the dream destination of thousands of software engineers, the stories of young Vietnamese people achieving success here are always a strong source of inspiration.</p><p>One of the notable stories is the journey of Tuan Linh, an excellent Android engineer, who joined the TikTok team in Singapore after studying and training at Engineer Pro.</p><p>In an interview with Engineer Pro, Tuan Linh not only shared about the challenges and experiences he has experienced, but also provided valuable advice for those who are aspiring to pursue careers at leading technology companies. Let's explore his story through the article below!</p><p><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/img/stories/anh-linh-tiktok-img1.webp\" title=\"\"/></p><h2>Hello Linh, thank you for taking the time to share your story. Can you introduce a little about yourself and your journey to TikTok?</h2><p>Hello everyone! My name is Tuan Linh, currently working at TikTok Singapore as a Software Engineer. Before joining TikTok, I had nearly 2 years of experience working in Android development in Vietnam.<br/>Initially, I didn't think I would have the opportunity to work at a large technology company like TikTok. But with effort and perseverance, along with cultivating knowledge and skills through courses at Engineer Pro, I achieved my goal. This is truly a big turning point in my career, helping me discover my abilities as well as open up many new opportunities in the future.</p><h2>It is known that he is a former student at Engineer Pro. Anh có thể chia sẻ quá trình học tập tại đây không?</h2><p>I learned about Engineer Pro by chance, through videos sharing programming skills and interviews on YouTube. The content here attracts me because it is very practical, easy to understand and close to the needs of those who want to apply to large companies. After a while of monitoring, I decided to sign up for a trial course.</p><p>I started with the DSA 2 course, I learned how to solve more complex algorithmic problems and optimize thinking. The course helps me not only understand the theory but also know how to apply it to specific interview situations. After completing DSA 2, I continued to participate in the DSA 3 course - going deeper into math problems at a difficult level and close to the requirements of large companies like TikTok.</p><p>What impresses me most about Engineer Pro is the clear learning path, scientific teaching methods, and especially the team of very dedicated mentors. They not only guided me in solving exercises but also helped me understand how to think and analyze problems, which I find extremely important when interviewing.</p><h2>Can you share what the interview process is like at TikTok?</h2><p>The interview process at TikTok is divided into 4 rounds, each round has a specific assessment goal:</p><ol><li>Online Assessment: This is an online programming test, often focusing on algorithmic problems. The requirement in this round is that you must optimize the time and space of the solutions.</li><li>HR Interview: This round is mainly about discussing career orientation, the position you are applying for, and learning about the company culture and job requirements.<br/></li><li>Three rounds of programming interviews (Coding Rounds):<br/></li></ol><ul><li>Round 1: They test their basic technical knowledge of CS Fundamentals. I was asked about basic data structures, algorithms, and how to apply them to real-life situations.</li><li>Round 2: This is a round about System Design. They asked me to design a specific system, from analyzing requirements to providing architectural solutions. What matters in this round is your ability to communicate and explain the solution.</li><li>Round 3: This round combines algorithmic and technical problems related to mobile development, especially Android. They want to test both the depth and breadth of expertise.</li></ul><ol><li>Final interview round: This is the round to evaluate soft skills and behavioral reflexes. They pose specific situations to see how they solve problems in a real work environment.</li></ol><p>I realize that CS Fundamentals is a very important factor at TikTok. Interviewers not only want to know how you solve problems, but also want to understand how you think and analyze problems.</p><h2>How did you prepare to pass these interview rounds?</h2><p>Preparation is very important, and I have divided it into three main stages:</p><ol><li>Prepare your CV: Your CV is the first step to impress employers. I consulted many video tutorials on writing a CV on YouTube, and asked the mentor at Engineer Pro to review and comment. I try to highlight the projects I've worked on and skills that match the position I'm applying for.</li><li>Practicing programming: I spend a lot of time practicing algorithm problems on LeetCode, especially medium and hard problems. Besides, I regularly conduct mock interviews to improve my reflexes and explanation skills when answering questions.</li><li>Behavioral Preparation (Behavioral Questions): This part requires you to have good communication skills and react quickly to hypothetical situations.  </li></ol><p>Thanks to my thorough preparation, I was much more confident when entering each interview round.</p><h2>After working at TikTok, did you encounter any difficulties?</h2><p>I have been working at TikTok for more than a week and this is also the first time I have moved from Vietnam to Singapore. At first, I was worried about integrating into the new working environment, but TikTok supported me a lot during the onboarding process.</p><p>I was provided with full documents and tools to start work, and the team was very open and ready to answer all questions. This helps me quickly get used to the job and feel more comfortable in the new environment.</p><h2>Do you have any advice for those who want to apply to TikTok or other large companies?</h2><p>My advice is:</p><ul><li>Focus on foundational skills: Algorithms, system design, and basic engineering are the three most important elements.</li><li>Persevere: Don't be discouraged if you fail the first few times. Every interview is a lesson for you to improve.</li><li>Build a clear learning path: If you don't know where to start, join reputable courses like Engineer Pro. Here, you not only learn knowledge but also receive support from a strong community.</li></ul><p>Thank you Linh for sharing your story! Engineer Pro wishes him more success at TikTok and on his upcoming career journey.</p>"
