    "originalTitleEn": "Necessary Skills For Senior Software Engineer At Big Tech",
    "originalHtmlEn": "<h2>Necessary Skills For Senior Software Engineer At Big Tech</h2><p>During Engineer Pro's regular webinar, two guests, Mr. Chan Thanh - Staff Engineer at TikTok, and Huy - Senior Software Engineer at Shopee, shared about the skills needed for a Senior Software Engineer at large technology companies. The discussion helps clarify the career development journey, important skills and how to approach the domestic and foreign job market.  </p><p>Details:  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=62RuV8iNZS4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=62RuV8iNZS4</a> </p><h2>Hello Thanh and Huy! Can you two share about your career journey and your experiences working at large technology companies?</h2><p>Huy: I started my career at Zalo, where I worked with many new technologies in a very dynamic but also stressful environment. After that, I moved to work at a small startup, where I had the opportunity to learn many different aspects but lacked guidance from experienced people. Next, I joined Garena, now Sea Group, a more professional environment, where I worked with many good engineers. Finally, I joined Shopee, where I was exposed to large and complex systems, helping me practice and develop more technical skills.</p><p>Thanh: I also started at Zalo, where I had access to large technologies and projects right from the beginning of my career. After that, I moved to Garena, I learned a lot about professional work, project management skills and large system development. After a while, I continued my career in a leadership and management role at a large company, where I learned how to develop teams and be responsible for products at a strategic level.</p><h2>According to you two, what are the most important skills to become a Senior Software Engineer at Big Tech?</h2><p>Thanh: In my opinion, there are three core skills that a Senior Software Engineer needs:</p><h3>1. Self-study</h3><ul><li>Technology changes very quickly, so the ability to self-study is a must.</li><li>Actively learn about new frameworks and libraries, follow technology blogs like Medium, Dev.to, Hacker News.</li><li>Read in-depth documents and don't be afraid to use translation tools to access knowledge from many different sources.</li></ul><h3>2. Be proactive and responsible</h3><ul><li>Don't just follow requests, but proactively propose improvements and optimizations to the system.</li><li>View work as a personal project, with responsibility from start to finish instead of just doing assigned tasks.</li><li>Take responsibility for product quality, ensure all features operate stably, do not blame others.</li></ul><h3>3. Communication</h3><ul><li>Communication is not only the exchange of information, but also the ability to clarify requirements and propose solutions.</li><li>Work with product managers and designers to understand product needs and optimize technical solutions.</li><li>Explain the problem clearly, ensuring all stakeholders understand correctly.</li><li>Proactively lead discussions, demonstrate leadership ability even without a management title.</li></ul><h2>For those who have just graduated or are at the Junior Engineer level, do you have any advice?</h2><p>Huy: If you just graduated, focus on the following:</p><ul><li>Apply many skills, not only learn theory but also need a lot of practice.</li><li>Self-study and practice interview skills, especially if you want to apply to large companies.</li><li>Choose a company with an environment that matches your development orientation.</li><li>Improve your foreign language skills to increase your opportunities to work at international companies.</li></ul><h2>If you want to find work opportunities abroad, especially in Singapore, what do candidates need to prepare?</h2><p>Thanh:</p><h3>Popular programming language</h3><ul><li>The Go language is widely used in large technology companies such as Shopee and Grab.</li><li>If you want to work in backend development, mastering Go can be a big advantage.</li></ul><h3>Job opportunities in Singapore</h3><ul><li>Companies in Singapore look for candidates with solid technical skills, outstanding interview performance and good English proficiency.</li><li>Good preparation in algorithms, design systems and communication will give you an advantage when applying to the international market.</li></ul><h2>Can you two share how to study effectively and manage time better?</h2><p>Huy:</p><ul><li>Study regularly, have a long-term plan instead of studying all at once.</li><li>Read in-depth articles and practice, actively program according to examples, test new technologies.</li><li>Select knowledge suitable for the job, avoid wandering.</li><li>Update technology trends, attend seminars, read specialized documents.</li><li>Participate in many interviews to improve your skills and understand market needs.</li></ul><h2>To advance and develop a long-term career, what do candidates need to keep in mind?</h2><p>Thanh:</p><h3>Internal promotion</h3><ul><li>To get promoted, you must have good results, strive regularly and clearly understand the company's goals.</li><li>Suggesting initiatives and contributing to the company's development will help you make an impression on management.</li></ul><h3>Apply for jobs outside the company</h3><ul><li>If you want to find opportunities at another company, prepare carefully with interview skills.</li><li>Demonstrate good technical ability and clear presentation skills.</li></ul><h2>Do you have any advice for those of you who are on the journey to becoming a Senior Engineer?</h2><p>Huy: If you want to become a Senior Software Engineer at Big Tech, always proactively learn, be responsible at work and practice communication skills.</p><p>Thanh: Don't just focus on coding, but develop systems thinking and leadership abilities. When you do those things well, opportunities will naturally come to you.</p><p>Hopefully these shares will help many of you conquer your Big Tech dreams!</p><p>_________________________________</p><p>EngineerPro is a training center with in-depth courses for software engineers. With 100% of instructors coming from Big Tech such as Google, Amazon, Shopee, TikTok,... EngineerPro ensures quality teaching and a clear learning path, from basic to advanced, helping students confidently apply for software engineer positions in this technology industry.  </p>"
